From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:31:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk: fragment shader state emitted only when it changes, bind
 counts

CS2's depth prepass costs ~110 us per draw call with no barrier or
cache invalidate recorded between the calls.  Every fragment shader bind
re-emitted, besides the program, SET_SUBTILING_PERF_KNOB_A/B,
SET_API_MANDATED_EARLY_Z, SET_POST_Z_PS_IMASK, SET_ZCULL_BOUNDS and the
NVK_MME_SET_SHADING_RATE_CONTROL and NVK_MME_SET_ANTI_ALIAS macros, even
when they were the same; a pass that alternates between shaders writes
early-Z and ZCULL bounds state between draws.

NVK_FS_STATE_TRACKING (default on, =0 restores the old stream): the state
after a fragment shader's program (nvk_shader::fs_tail_dw_start) is
emitted only when it differs from the last one emitted in the command
buffer.  Meta operations, generated commands and secondaries forget it
(nvk_cmd_forget_gfx_gpu_state), so the next bind emits it in full.  The
macros merge their parameter with other state kept in MME scratch, which
the skipped call would have left unchanged.

NVK_PASS_PROFILE: each pass's shaders line also counts the shader stage
programs emitted (and of them fragment shaders) and the descriptor set /
descriptor buffer offset binds per pass.

Constant buffers bound from CPU-known addresses are already skipped when
unchanged (0004); with NVK_UBO_DESC_CBUF=0, the Windows default, UBO
descriptors are not bound through NVK_MME_BIND_CBUF_DESC at all.

No MME macro change: 2160 dwords for a DXVK device.

NVK_PASS_PROFILE=4 also says, per pass, how many index buffer binds,
vertex buffer binds and indirect draw calls point into system memory and
into BAR-heap VRAM (the placement of the memory whose own VA holds the
address, from the device's memory list): 405.15's histogram shows an
index and a vertex buffer rebind before every indirect call of CS2's
depth prepass, and with the BAR heap off (0030) host-visible buffers are
system memory the GPU fetches across PCIe.
---
